      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li>Street works in England and Wales fall under the New Roads and Street Works Act 1991 (NRSWA). In England reinstatements follow the DfT Specification for the Reinstatement of Openings in Highways (SROH).</li><li>Inspections follow the DfT Code of Practice for Street Works Inspections. A defect can mean putting the work right, so check the Code.</li><li>Many operatives never fill in a separate app on site. They do it later from memory.</li><li>Quickler charges £75 per month per phone number & unlimited free dashboard accounts.</li><li>Quickler records the proof. It does not lay the reinstatement.</li></ul>"
