      "html": "<p>In England and Wales the New Roads and Street Works Act 1991 governs works in the highway. The Specification for the Reinstatement of Openings in Highways (SROH) sets materials, layer depths and compaction, and gives road categories. Many authorities also run permit schemes.</p><p>Quickler records the permit reference, category, layers and coring results, with photos taken there and then. The office sees the status without chasing. It does not lay the reinstatement.</p>"
