      "html": "<p>NRSWA 1991 Part III is headed street works in England and Wales. Section 71 requires reinstatement to meet prescribed requirements for materials, workmanship and performance, and section 67 requires supervision by a person with a prescribed qualification and a trained operative on site; both apply to England and Wales. The DfT published the fourth edition of the SROH as statutory guidance in force from 10 May 2021 (via search), and Scotland uses its own specification, the SROR. The gov.uk Code of Practice for Street Works Inspections is dated April 2023, but its text could not be read here, so the page no longer states inspection categories, coring rules, remedial notices or inspection charges, and whether the SROH applies the same way in Wales was not checked. Official sources checked on 18 November 2026.</p><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/1991/22/section/71\" rel=\"noopener\">New Roads and Street Works Act 1991 section 71 (legislation.gov.uk)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/1991/22/section/67\" rel=\"noopener\">New Roads and Street Works Act 1991 section 67 (legislation.gov.uk)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/specification-for-the-reinstatement-of-openings-in-highways\" rel=\"noopener\">Specification for the Reinstatement of Openings in Highways (gov.uk)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/643579a1877741001368d7f8/code-of-practice-for-street-works-inspections-april-2023.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\">Code of Practice for Street Works Inspections, April 2023 (gov.uk)</a></li></ul>"
